   - `horizon_topology` in F1 only — WCC-specific.
   - `numeric multiset differs` is a false-positive trigger for text like "l1" (letter+digit → NUM_RE catches "1") and dates "-04" from "2026-09-12T..." Hmm "hypotheses_reconciliation" numbers come from a timestamp inside text. Very noisy.
   
   So the meaningful signal is: the *shared core* fields (equations, matter, Lambda, constraints, s, delta, decay rates, slice topology, spacetime dimension) are identical; differences are either (a) class-defining (extension regularity C0/C2/none, extension topology, class-specific warnings) or (b) editorial/provenance.

